: 44.026}], "sentences": [{"text": "Did you know Vikings forged swords using metallurgy Europe wouldn't rediscover for 800 years?", "s": 0.05, "e": 7.315}, {"text": "Between 800 and 1000 AD, elite Norse warriors carried blades stamped with the name \"Ulfberht.\"", "s": 7.495, "e": 15.368}, {"text": "While ordinary European swords were brittle and bent in battle, Ulfberht swords were made of crucible steel, a metal heated to over 3,000 degrees Fahrenheit to strip out impurities.", "s": 15.488, "e": 28.829}, {"text": "Historians believe Vikings traded furs and amber along Russian river routes to get raw steel ingots from Central Asia.", "s": 28.949, "e": 37.606}, {"text": "Because they were nearly unbreakable, counterfeit versions flooded the market with misspelled names.", "s": 37.726, "e": 44.026}]}